source: crates/leptoskit_cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "normalize(&stdout(&output), &scratch.path)"
---
Reproduce and package a backend without rebuilding it in the image

Usage: leptoskit infra build-verified [OPTIONS] --bundle <BUNDLE> --manifest <MANIFEST> --sha256 <SHA256> --runtime-image <RUNTIME_IMAGE> --runtime-config-sha256 <RUNTIME_CONFIG_SHA256> --tag <TAG> --out <OUT>

Options:
      --bundle <BUNDLE>
          The extracted backend bundle directory

      --manifest <MANIFEST>
          The inventory written with the bundle

      --sha256 <SHA256>
          The expected inventory digest, obtained independently of the bundle

      --checkout <CHECKOUT>
          Compare the source with this local clone instead of fetching the recipe's commit from its repository

      --offline
          Skip the steps that need the network: fetching the commit and re-resolving dependencies. Only the executable is rebuilt

      --engine <ENGINE>
          The container engine. Defaults to docker, then podman, whichever responds

          Possible values:
          - docker: Docker
          - podman: Podman

      --runtime-image <RUNTIME_IMAGE>
          Digest-pinned runtime image (not a mutable tag)

      --runtime-config-sha256 <RUNTIME_CONFIG_SHA256>
          Independently selected SHA-256 of the runtime image's Config JSON

      --tag <TAG>
          Local image tag. This command never pushes

      --reuse-existing
          Inspect an existing local tag instead of packaging a new image

      --no-rpc
          Explicit operator declaration that this backend exposes no RPC API

      --out <OUT>
          New descriptor file, written only after image extraction succeeds

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
